Spec: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/spec.md (Store: writers and readers; supports AC56, AC57)
ADR: docs/decisions/0004-capture-store.md
Research: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/research.md Q9 (mode=ro on a stopped WAL database creates -wal/-shm, leaves gateway.db's mtime alone; immutable=1 rejected)
Why this approach: OpenReader stats gateway.db before the driver sees it, so a missing store is an fs.ErrNotExist error naming the path and nothing is created. The DSN is mode=ro plus busy_timeout, built through url.URL like the writer's. The reader checks user_version and never migrates. Content validates the hash shape (64 lowercase hex) before any lookup, so no caller string reaches a blob path, and checks the decoded size against the row. Events reads existence and rows in one read transaction, ordered by seq. Row types carry column-named JSON tags for dump's one-line output.
Alternatives rejected: immutable=1 (torn reads while the gateway writes, Q9); letting the driver open a missing file (it would create gateway.db); treating an unknown exchange in Events as an empty list (dump needs ErrNotFound to exit 1).
Trade-off / known limit: against a stopped gateway SQLite still creates gateway.db-wal and -shm (Q9). Last() orders by started_at, ties to rowid. A reader refuses a database older than the binary; the gateway migrates it on its next start. Recorded in plan.md ("Details fixed in T12").
Verified by: make verify; go test -race ./internal/store -run TestReader (TestReader_MissingStoreNotCreated empty_dir and missing_dir, TestReader_StoppedStore with mtime/size unchanged and only -wal/-shm new, TestReader_WhileWriterOpen with 30 deadline-bound writes beside a looping reader, TestReader_UnknownID incl. a path-traversal hash); tests first failed to build on the missing API.
